  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a medium saucepan of water to the boil for the noodles. Coarsely chop the cabbage. Thinly slice the spring onion, keeping the white and green parts separate. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3582457/photos/large/124525_1-2d31200797bee55000e6a08a060f171b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make sauce: Put the garlic, peanut butter, Chinese barbecue seasoning, 2 tbs soy sauce, 1 tbs white vinegar, 2 tsp sugar and 1½ tbs water in a bowl and stir until well combined.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3582463/photos/large/124525_2-37ec8cf658eabe4584c0b89cdfca1b86.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook noodles: Cook the noodles in the pan of boiling water for 7 mins or until tender. Drain, then rinse under hot water to prevent the noodles from sticking. Return the noodles to the pan, add 2 tsp vegetable oil and toss to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3582467/photos/large/124525_3-6f8bad9adaf1099958dce286fae6cf2b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook plant-based mince: Meanwhile, heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium deep frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the plant-based mince, breaking up the lumps with a spoon, for 5-6 mins until browned. Add the cabbage, sauce and white part of the spring onion and cook, stirring, for 1 min or until the sauce is thickened. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3582468/photos/large/124525_4-893ff8d40ebad710a450bbff68d3e9c5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the noodles and mince mixture among bowls. Scatter over the fried shallots and remaining spring onion. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3582469/photos/large/124525_5-6ad1770c5fea8dcfe15c86ac6e3f33fa.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Did you know?: Dan dan noodles is an iconic Sichuan street food. It's typically made with pork mince, preserved vegetables, chilli oil, spices and sesame paste, but we've used peanut butter for a delicious spin on this classic dish.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3582470/photos/large/124525_6-451cc7fd1870d344ce8d42ec7dc6db5c.jpeg"
    }
  ]
